# Claim ledger

Every claim in the abstract, introduction and conclusion, and every number in the text and
tables, with the theorem/section or figure/table that supports it and the results file it is
read from. Numbers enter the text only as macros generated into `numbers.tex` by
`tools/make_numbers.py` from `results/` (delivered by experiment-repo); figures and tables are
delivered by figtab-repo under `paper/figures/` and `paper/tables/` from scripts in `code/figures/`.

Status (2026-10-18): the theory section (Sec. 4, App. A) is written from experiment-repo's
derivation note `theory/derivations.md` rev. 2 (a61cb8a); E1 (Sec. 6.1) is written from
`results/e1/` (experiment-repo 883c59d). E1 is a **development set** (the capture rule was fixed
after quick runs on it). E1b (Sec. 6.2) is the **held-out, pre-registered** linear test, written from
`results/e1b/` (experiment-repo 4b0cd29; predictions committed at 0576788 before any run); rank is read at
convergence there, so E1b tests the rank at t_end (experiment-repo 3e31766: 'rank at t_end', long-horizon rank beside it; for λ>0 final in 544 of 555 checked runs, `all_lam>0`). E2 (Sec. 6.3) is written from `results/e2/` (experiment-repo 9d38b08; predictions committed at db2a53b before any run); E3 commits `results/e3/prediction.json` before its runs. Theory corrections of experiment-repo 2b74aed are in: Prop. 1 and Cor. 3 credit the per-mode system and integral of Tian et al. 2021 (their eqs. 11-12, 14); the α=1 critical weight decay is eq. (13), λ_k^race ≈ h_k(p0)/log(p0/a0); the no-predictor limit is stated for equal-marginal views, with the Bernoulli-mask exception (App. B). The plan is story-repo
`plan.md` v1 (dff5a341). A claim the evidence does not support is weakened or dropped here and in the text.

